Boudewijn Waijers wrote:
> Every dragon is good to eat, since all give a full tummy. Most give an
> intrinsic as well (100% guaranteed or your money back).
> 
> White gives cold resistance, red fire, orange sleep, yellow poison (but
> HP loss from eating as well),

	It's the greens that provide poison resistance. I don't actually
recall if their meat is poison, but eating them is safe if you're
already poison resistant, at least (which I always am by the time I
start running into them, which is why I don't remember if they're
poisonous).

	Yellows are acid-breathers, and eating them *doesn't* provide
acid resistance (but it counters stoning), and does do acid damage.

 > blue shock (which you still don't have),
> and black disintegration, the most valued resistance, since black
> dragons may otherwise kill you with a single breath (barring armour
> layers).

	Of the dragon resistances, disintegration is probably the one I
value *least*. Barring really stupid behaviour, disintegration
resistance only helps against black dragons' breath weapon, which can be
nullified by reflection, which I've almost always got by the time I
start running into them.

	The others protect against not just reflectable dragon breath,
but non-reflectable attacks from various monsters and traps, and the
things they protect against start showing up much earlier. I think shock
resistance is actually the one I value most... energy vortices are
*lethal* if you don't have it. Running into gnomes with wands of
lightning before you have reflection hurts, too.

	My monk ascended without disintegration resistance (it's really
hard to get as a vegan), and never missed it. I'm quite sure that she
would've been dead several times over without shock resistance.

> Only silver dragons and grey dragons give no intrinsic when you eat
> them. Then again, those two provide the most valued armour (probably
> because the intrinsics offered by those aren't available as intrinsics).

	And yellow. If you've already got reflection and magic
resistance from other sources, YDSM isn't a bad deal. All the other
dragon-scale resistances can be gotten intrinsically, but acid
resistance is hard to come by.

